From fc78a2167025662ba7469b02147130004a34f479 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 08:49:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add native iOS app for DiscVault
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Full SwiftUI iOS app (Swift 6, iOS 18+ deployment target) that connects
to the existing Flask backend over REST/JWT.

First-launch onboarding flow:
- WelcomeView: branded splash with feature highlights
- ServerSetupView: enter & test server URL before proceeding to login
  (also accessible from Profile and Admin Settings for editing)

Architecture:
- AppStateManager drives the app phase (welcome → serverSetup → login → main)
- APIClient (@Observable) handles all REST calls with auto token refresh
- KeychainService stores tokens, server URL and username securely
- MVVM: CollectionViewModel, MovieDetailViewModel, AuthViewModel

Screens:
- LoginView: username/password + server URL link
- MainTabView: Collection, Lists, Scan, Search, Profile tabs
- CollectionView: 3-column grid with filter/sort sheet and barcode add flow
- MovieDetailView: hero backdrop, actions, cast scroll, plot
- BarcodeScannerView: AVFoundation EAN-13/UPC-A scanner with torch
- SearchView: debounced live search
- ListsView: Watchlist + Watch History with swipe-to-delete
- ProfileView: user info, groups, server URL edit, sign out
- AdminSettingsView: DB stats, server URL editor, connection test

Xcode project (iOS 18 deployment, bundle nl.zandbergenonline.DiscVault)
includes all source files and Assets.xcassets.

